[{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4162043057","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/118030#issuecomment-4162043057","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/118030","id":4162043057,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc74E7yx","user":{"login":"Alzurana","id":7355313,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjczNTUzMTM=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/7355313?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Alzurana","html_url":"https://github.com/Alzurana","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Alzurana/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Alzurana/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Alzurana/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Alzurana/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Alzurana/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Alzurana/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Alzurana/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Alzurana/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Alzurana/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-03-31T11:45:39Z","updated_at":"2026-03-31T11:45:39Z","body":"Fixed that function name, it fits the convention way better, now. And formatter also worked this time","author_association":"NONE","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4162043057/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4164855898","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/118030#issuecomment-4164855898","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/118030","id":4164855898,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc74Pqha","user":{"login":"WhalesState","id":53877170,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjUzODc3MTcw","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/53877170?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/WhalesState","html_url":"https://github.com/WhalesState","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WhalesState/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WhalesState/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WhalesState/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WhalesState/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WhalesState/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WhalesState/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WhalesState/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WhalesState/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WhalesState/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-03-31T19:14:06Z","updated_at":"2026-03-31T19:31:52Z","body":"Replacing `step_decimals(double)` with this fixes the issue without adding a new method.\r\n\r\n```c++\r\nint Math::step_decimals(double p_value) {\r\n\tdouble abs_value = p_value >= 0.0 ? p_value : -p_value;\r\n\tint decimal_count = 0;\r\n\twhile (decimal_count < 15) {\r\n\t\tif (abs_value - (int)abs_value < 1e-9) {\r\n\t\t\treturn decimal_count;\r\n\t\t}\r\n\t\tabs_value *= 10.0;\r\n\t\tdecimal_count++;\r\n\t}\r\n\treturn decimal_count;\r\n}\r\n```","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4164855898/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4165088413","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/118030#issuecomment-4165088413","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/118030","id":4165088413,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc74QjSd","user":{"login":"YeldhamDev","id":30739239,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjMwNzM5MjM5","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/30739239?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/YeldhamDev","html_url":"https://github.com/YeldhamDev","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/YeldhamDev/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/YeldhamDev/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/YeldhamDev/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/YeldhamDev/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/YeldhamDev/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/YeldhamDev/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/YeldhamDev/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/YeldhamDev/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/YeldhamDev/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-03-31T19:54:33Z","updated_at":"2026-03-31T19:57:14Z","body":"@WhalesState That would alter the behavior of `step_decimals()`, which is exposed, and explicitly states that returns the first non-zero digit's position. Unless I'm misunderstanding it.","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4165088413/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":1,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4165150841","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/118030#issuecomment-4165150841","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/118030","id":4165150841,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc74Qyh5","user":{"login":"Alzurana","id":7355313,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjczNTUzMTM=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/7355313?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Alzurana","html_url":"https://github.com/Alzurana","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Alzurana/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Alzurana/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Alzurana/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Alzurana/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Alzurana/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Alzurana/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Alzurana/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Alzurana/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Alzurana/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-03-31T20:06:35Z","updated_at":"2026-03-31T20:15:48Z","body":"@YeldhamDev That is correct. step_decimals does exactly what it also states in the documentation, returning the position of the first significant digit after the decimal point. It actually returns the abs of the negative exponent for it's input floats fraction if it were written in scientific notation. 0.004 returns 3 which is the same as 4e-3\r\n\r\nI suspect, since there is no function to actually count the amount of significant digits, people might have confused it for one.\r\n\r\nAlso, I implemented your changes","author_association":"NONE","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4165150841/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":1,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4165237507","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/118030#issuecomment-4165237507","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/118030","id":4165237507,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc74RHsD","user":{"login":"YeldhamDev","id":30739239,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjMwNzM5MjM5","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/30739239?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/YeldhamDev","html_url":"https://github.com/YeldhamDev","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/YeldhamDev/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/YeldhamDev/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/YeldhamDev/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/YeldhamDev/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/YeldhamDev/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/YeldhamDev/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/YeldhamDev/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/YeldhamDev/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/YeldhamDev/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-03-31T20:17:34Z","updated_at":"2026-03-31T20:17:34Z","body":"I would also recommend exposing it to scripting, as I bet this could be useful for the engine users as well.","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4165237507/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4165617863","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/118030#issuecomment-4165617863","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/118030","id":4165617863,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc74SkjH","user":{"login":"WhalesState","id":53877170,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjUzODc3MTcw","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/53877170?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/WhalesState","html_url":"https://github.com/WhalesState","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WhalesState/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WhalesState/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WhalesState/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WhalesState/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WhalesState/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WhalesState/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WhalesState/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WhalesState/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WhalesState/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-03-31T21:11:39Z","updated_at":"2026-03-31T21:11:39Z","body":"> @WhalesState That would alter the behavior of `step_decimals()`, which is exposed, and explicitly states that returns the first non-zero digit's position. Unless I'm misunderstanding it.\r\n\r\nYes, I just saw the docs, sorry about that.\r\n\r\nI have checked the new `count_decimals` method from this PR and it always return `6` on godbolt, also my prev method wasn't also accurate due to how doubles are stored so the result for `0.0005` was `4` but `1.0005` was `15`.\r\nhttps://godbolt.org/z/s7MsrKbrd\r\n\r\nAnyways, here's the same implementation for my prev method after fixing the precision which should gives accurate results and is also capped to 6 instead of 15.\r\n\r\n```c++\r\nint Math::count_decimals(double p_value) {\r\n\tdouble abs_value = abs(p_value);\r\n\tint decimal_count = 0;\r\n\twhile (decimal_count < 6) {\r\n\t\tdouble diff = abs_value - (int)(abs_value + 0.5);\r\n\t\tif (diff < 1e-9 && diff > -1e-9) {\r\n\t\t\treturn decimal_count;\r\n\t\t}\r\n\t\tabs_value *= 10.0;\r\n\t\tdecimal_count++;\r\n\t}\r\n\treturn decimal_count;\r\n}\r\n```","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4165617863/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4166314401","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/118030#issuecomment-4166314401","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/118030","id":4166314401,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc74VOmh","user":{"login":"Alzurana","id":7355313,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjczNTUzMTM=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/7355313?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Alzurana","html_url":"https://github.com/Alzurana","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Alzurana/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Alzurana/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Alzurana/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Alzurana/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Alzurana/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Alzurana/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Alzurana/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Alzurana/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Alzurana/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-03-31T23:26:11Z","updated_at":"2026-03-31T23:28:01Z","body":"Hey @WhalesState your function could work up to 10 decimals.\r\n\r\nConsidering this function might be exposed to GDScript it would make sense to work with doubles as that's what variant uses with exceptions on vectors and some other types. We could add a parameter to select the maximum allowed depth if someone wants to shove a float into it.\r\n\r\n``` c++\r\nint Math::count_decimals(double p_value, int p_max = 10) {\r\n\tp_max = min(p_max, 10);\r\n    double abs_value = abs(p_value);\r\n\tint decimal_count = 0;\r\n\twhile (decimal_count < p_max) {\r\n\t\tdouble diff = abs_value - (int)(abs_value + 0.5);\r\n\t\tif (diff < 1e-9 && diff > -1e-9) {\r\n\t\t\treturn decimal_count;\r\n\t\t}\r\n\t\tabs_value *= 10.0;\r\n\t\tdecimal_count++;\r\n\t}\r\n\treturn decimal_count;\r\n}\r\n```","author_association":"NONE","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4166314401/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":1,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4166437070","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/118030#issuecomment-4166437070","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/118030","id":4166437070,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc74VsjO","user":{"login":"WhalesState","id":53877170,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjUzODc3MTcw","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/53877170?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/WhalesState","html_url":"https://github.com/WhalesState","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WhalesState/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WhalesState/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WhalesState/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WhalesState/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WhalesState/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WhalesState/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WhalesState/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WhalesState/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WhalesState/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-03-31T23:54:38Z","updated_at":"2026-03-31T23:54:38Z","body":"> Hey @WhalesState your function could work up to 10 decimals.\r\n> \r\n> Considering this function might be exposed to GDScript it would make sense to work with doubles as that's what variant uses with exceptions on vectors and some other types. We could add a parameter to select the maximum allowed depth if someone wants to shove a float into it.\r\n\r\nI’d recommend using `real_t` for better consistency with Godot. By default, Godot uses `float` unless it’s compiled with `double` precision, so `real_t` is much better for exposed methods.\r\n\r\nAlso I don't see a use-case for exposing this method but it can be faster than converting a float to string and counting the digits after the decimal point.","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4166437070/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4166484944","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/118030#issuecomment-4166484944","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/118030","id":4166484944,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc74V4PQ","user":{"login":"WhalesState","id":53877170,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjUzODc3MTcw","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/53877170?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/WhalesState","html_url":"https://github.com/WhalesState","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WhalesState/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WhalesState/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WhalesState/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WhalesState/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WhalesState/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WhalesState/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WhalesState/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WhalesState/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WhalesState/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-04-01T00:05:32Z","updated_at":"2026-04-01T00:05:32Z","body":"Also when using `real_t`, `p_max` can be determined locally for each build using `#ifdef USE_DOUBLE_PRECISION`, and clamping it can be done easily for the returned value using `mini()` method so we don't need an extra argument for now, since removing it in the future after any discussion will break compatibility.","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4166484944/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4169546307","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/118030#issuecomment-4169546307","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/118030","id":4169546307,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc74hjpD","user":{"login":"Alzurana","id":7355313,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjczNTUzMTM=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/7355313?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Alzurana","html_url":"https://github.com/Alzurana","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Alzurana/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Alzurana/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Alzurana/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Alzurana/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Alzurana/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Alzurana/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Alzurana/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Alzurana/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Alzurana/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-04-01T11:53:19Z","updated_at":"2026-04-01T11:53:19Z","body":"@WhalesState What do you think of this behavior?\r\n\r\nhttps://godbolt.org/z/Gazx35c4z\r\n\r\nUncomment the define at the very top to see double vs float behavior","author_association":"NONE","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4169546307/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4169670439","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/118030#issuecomment-4169670439","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/118030","id":4169670439,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc74iB8n","user":{"login":"WhalesState","id":53877170,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjUzODc3MTcw","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/53877170?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/WhalesState","html_url":"https://github.com/WhalesState","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WhalesState/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WhalesState/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WhalesState/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WhalesState/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WhalesState/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WhalesState/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WhalesState/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WhalesState/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WhalesState/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-04-01T12:16:44Z","updated_at":"2026-04-01T12:24:14Z","body":"looks fine but you will need to fix the precision for values greater than 0, check the second method that i have pasted here.\n\n![Screenshot_20260401-140850_Brave.jpg](https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/8f05a454-7857-4599-a58d-8f9fc24a16bc)\n\n\n\n\n\n    ","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4169670439/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4172865645","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/118030#issuecomment-4172865645","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/118030","id":4172865645,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc74uOBt","user":{"login":"Alzurana","id":7355313,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjczNTUzMTM=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/7355313?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Alzurana","html_url":"https://github.com/Alzurana","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Alzurana/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Alzurana/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Alzurana/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Alzurana/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Alzurana/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Alzurana/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Alzurana/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Alzurana/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Alzurana/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-04-01T20:45:48Z","updated_at":"2026-04-01T20:49:44Z","body":"Hello there.\r\n\r\nI think I have arrived at a more elegant solution. Trying to work around float inaccuracies and trying to extract decimal digits from an inherently binary format that does not even map said digits was silly. The new solution scales the fraction up and deals with it as an integer.\r\nHere is a quick testing ground for it: https://godbolt.org/z/oErG3xjx5\r\n\r\nI added documentation and testing cases to the PR for review. The documentation helps to further solidify what this function is supposed to do.\r\n\r\n@WhalesState Are you sure this function should operate on a variable precision based on the build? step_digits only works with doubles and on the GDScript side any Variant float is a double as well. Only vectors remain floats. There might also be an argument to keep a pure 32 bit precision for this function as step_digits does as well. The documentation there states it was an explicit design choice, this might as well make sense, here, for usability. It's probably best to limit the range to 6 regardless of the build.","author_association":"NONE","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4172865645/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4173626496","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/118030#issuecomment-4173626496","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/118030","id":4173626496,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc74xHyA","user":{"login":"WhalesState","id":53877170,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjUzODc3MTcw","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/53877170?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/WhalesState","html_url":"https://github.com/WhalesState","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WhalesState/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WhalesState/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WhalesState/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WhalesState/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WhalesState/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WhalesState/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WhalesState/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WhalesState/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WhalesState/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-04-01T23:48:20Z","updated_at":"2026-04-02T00:34:31Z","body":"> @WhalesState Are you sure this function should operate on a variable precision based on the build?\r\n\r\nIMO, we should focus on solving the Spinbox rounding issue first and to keep it simple and fast using the best approach, we don't even need to expose it unless it reaches a stable state, so the priority for now is just to give accurate result up to (at least) 5 digits for `double` type.\r\n","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4173626496/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4193409431","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/118030#issuecomment-4193409431","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/118030","id":4193409431,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc758lmX","user":{"login":"Alzurana","id":7355313,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjczNTUzMTM=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/7355313?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Alzurana","html_url":"https://github.com/Alzurana","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Alzurana/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Alzurana/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Alzurana/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Alzurana/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Alzurana/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Alzurana/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Alzurana/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Alzurana/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Alzurana/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-04-06T16:15:00Z","updated_at":"2026-04-06T16:15:00Z","body":"@WhalesState \r\nOk, did everything. Took the function out of global scope. It's now precision agnostic (always double) and offers the same depth as step_decimals (precise up to 6 digits).","author_association":"NONE","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4193409431/reactions","total_count":2,"+1":1,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":1,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4205133837","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/118030#issuecomment-4205133837","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/118030","id":4205133837,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc76pUAN","user":{"login":"Alzurana","id":7355313,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjczNTUzMTM=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/7355313?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Alzurana","html_url":"https://github.com/Alzurana","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Alzurana/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Alzurana/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Alzurana/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Alzurana/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Alzurana/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Alzurana/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Alzurana/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Alzurana/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Alzurana/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-04-08T09:11:19Z","updated_at":"2026-04-08T09:11:19Z","body":"@YeldhamDev I was asked by WhalesState to keep it out of @GlobalScope for now","author_association":"NONE","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4205133837/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":1},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4206281416","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/118030#issuecomment-4206281416","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/118030","id":4206281416,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc76tsLI","user":{"login":"WhalesState","id":53877170,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjUzODc3MTcw","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/53877170?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/WhalesState","html_url":"https://github.com/WhalesState","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WhalesState/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WhalesState/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WhalesState/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WhalesState/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WhalesState/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WhalesState/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WhalesState/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WhalesState/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WhalesState/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-04-08T12:39:16Z","updated_at":"2026-04-08T12:39:16Z","body":"It was just my opinion, if it was reliable enough for large numbers i could have agreed on exposing it.\n\nAlso exposing methods usually needs a proposal and a use-case, so i only cared about merging the bug fix first and if anyone needed it for his project it will be easy to expose the method after discussing it's limitations.","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4206281416/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":1,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4206729025","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/118030#issuecomment-4206729025","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/118030","id":4206729025,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc76vZdB","user":{"login":"YeldhamDev","id":30739239,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjMwNzM5MjM5","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/30739239?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/YeldhamDev","html_url":"https://github.com/YeldhamDev","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/YeldhamDev/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/YeldhamDev/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/YeldhamDev/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/YeldhamDev/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/YeldhamDev/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/YeldhamDev/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/YeldhamDev/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/YeldhamDev/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/YeldhamDev/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-04-08T13:49:22Z","updated_at":"2026-04-08T13:49:22Z","body":"> Also exposing methods usually needs a proposal and a use-case\r\n\r\nI doubt such a small thing would need a full blown proposal. :stuck_out_tongue_closed_eyes:\r\nBut not exposing it is not a showstopper either, and can be done in a different PR.","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4206729025/reactions","total_count":3,"+1":3,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4207307613","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/118030#issuecomment-4207307613","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/118030","id":4207307613,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc76xmtd","user":{"login":"WhalesState","id":53877170,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjUzODc3MTcw","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/53877170?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/WhalesState","html_url":"https://github.com/WhalesState","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WhalesState/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WhalesState/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WhalesState/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WhalesState/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WhalesState/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WhalesState/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WhalesState/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WhalesState/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WhalesState/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-04-08T15:11:30Z","updated_at":"2026-04-08T15:11:30Z","body":"The devs who doesn't agree on exposing a method are always ready to explain their detailed technical reasons. 😁","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comm